Intermediate 22A. 5-Cyclopropyl-2-(1,1-dimethoxyethyl)thiazole: To a degassed solution of 5-bromo-2-(1,1-dimethoxyethyl)thiazole (0.500 g, 1.983 mmol), prepared using the procedure described in WO 2004/087699, and [1,1′-bis(diphenylphosphino) ferrocene]dichloropalladium (II) complex with dichloromethane (1:1) (0.162 g, 0.198 mmol) in THF (19.83 mL) was added cyclopropylzinc(II) bromide, 0.5 M in THF (19.83 mL, 9.92 mmol) and the reaction mixture was degassed an additional 3 times. The reaction mixture was then heated at 65° C. for 20 h, cooled to rt, diluted with water and extracted with EtOAc (3×). The combined organic phases were washed with brine, dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated. The residue was purified by flash chromatography (silica gel, hexanes:EtOAc, 100:0 to 70:30) to afford 0.327 g (77%) of Intermediate 22A as a yellow oil. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.48 (d, J=0.8 Hz, 1H), 3.25 (s, 6H), 2.10-1.96 (m, 1H), 1.70 (s, 3H), 1.09-0.96 (m, 2H), 0.78-0.66 (m, 2H). LCMS Anal. Calc'd for C10H15NO2S, 213.0. found [M+H-MeOH] 182.0.
