Intermediate 23A. 1-(5-Bromothiazol-2-yl)ethanone: To a solution of 5-bromo-2-(1,1-dimethoxyethyl)thiazole (0.828 g, 3.28 mmol) in DCM (3.90 mL) was added TFA (2.53 mL, 32.8 mmol) and water (0.195 mL) and the reaction mixture stirred at 23° C. under Ar at 1 atm for 2 h. The solvent was removed in vacuo (azeotroped with MeOH, 2×) and the residue was dissolved in DCM, washed with sat. NaHCO3, water and brine. The organic layer was dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, filtered, concentrated and air-dried under vacuum to give a crude product. The crude product was further purified by ISCO (Hex:EtOAc 0-20%) to give Intermediate 23A (640 mg, 3.11 mmol, 95% yield) as a crude light brown solid. LCMS Anal. Calc'd for C5H4BrNOS 204.9. found [M+H] 206.1.
